      {
        "id": 91271,
        "name": "PlatinumWarlock",
        "username": "PlatinumWarlock",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/platinumwarlock/{size}/1869_2.png",
        "created_at": "2014-02-14T01:57:06.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote group-playtesters\" data-username=\"UXM266\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/uxm266/48/1966_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> UXM266:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>I agree, it it's also in ThinkGeek's style of self-deprication and love for fun, especially alliteration!</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>Quoted for both truth and emphasis.</p>\n<p>ThinkGeek is full of self-deprecating humor. &nbsp;The fact that they coupled it with a Marvel reference speaks to their 'authentic nerdity'.</p>",
