      {
        "id": 91272,
        "name": "Envisioner",
        "username": "Envisioner",
        "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/e/9de053/{size}.png",
        "created_at": "2014-02-14T02:01:00.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>I have no problem with <em>self-</em>deprecation, as long as it's not <em>my</em>self being deprecated by somebody <em>else</em>, which is what this copy reads like to me.&nbsp; <em>Self</em>-deprecation would be something like \"We at ThinkGeek have so little to do with our time, we just sit around playing SOTM all day...it's pretty awesome, so even if you do have an actual life, you should still check it out\".&nbsp; I would have had no problem with that message.</p>",
