      {
        "id": 91273,
        "name": "Silverleaf",
        "username": "Silverleaf",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/silverleaf/{size}/2332_2.png",
        "created_at": "2014-02-14T04:48:40.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>My point is, if you lose it's not an insult to describe you as a loser, <em>because you lost</em>. If you chose to be insulted by that, that's your choice, but it's still true. If you won, you're a winner. Simple. Same as you can describe me as white, British, female, gamer, musician, artist, non-German speaker, or whatever, and none of these things are insults. I have been the loser of many many games. That's fine.</p><p>We totally use \"loser\" in the UK, in the insulting rather than descriptive sense. And \"tosser\" means exactly the same \"jerk\" (and also \"wanker\"). \"Poof\"? We're going for homophobic insults now?</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p>",
        "post_number": 25,
        "post_type": 1,
