      {
        "id": 91276,
        "name": "UXM266",
        "username": "UXM266",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/uxm266/{size}/1966_2.png",
        "created_at": "2014-02-14T14:27:30.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>Essentially, ThinkGeek is one of the major hubs for buying cool geeky things. Having TG's monkeys (they call themselves that!) put a product on their site on their your product on there is an excellent mielstone!</p><p>I've bought a lot of cool stuff from them, and their &nbsp;customer service, style, and care has never let me down. We should not make a post about how TG describes products on their site.</p><p>We should all be buying &gt;G beer, shots, goblets of chocolate milk, what ahve you. This. Is super super super cool!</p><p>More importantly, we did know about and like this first. That doens't make su hipsters, that makes us ahve great taste!</p>",
